1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,743
Every report in Miftah is read from the
same

2
00:00:03,743 --> 00:00:07,487
ledger, so the reports always agree with
each other.

3
00:00:07,487 --> 00:00:11,230
As the Accountant, open Profit and Loss
for the

4
00:00:11,230 --> 00:00:14,974
year from 1 September 2025 to 31 August
2026.

5
00:00:14,974 --> 00:00:19,965
Rental income is 567,333.63: rent earned
day by day, not cash collected.

6
00:00:19,965 --> 00:00:22,461
Fees, parking, maintenance charges and the

7
00:00:22,461 --> 00:00:24,957
cheque return penalty sit beside it.

8
00:00:24,957 --> 00:00:28,700
The 5,000 recovered from a written-off
debt is other

9
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:32,444
income, and the write-off itself,
11,326.03, is an expense.

10
00:00:32,444 --> 00:00:36,603
Net operating income for the year is
494,787.54, and the

11
00:00:36,603 --> 00:00:40,347
badge confirms that the report ties to the
ledger.

12
00:00:40,347 --> 00:00:45,338
Open the Property Profit Report to see
each building on its own.

13
00:00:45,338 --> 00:00:49,497
Pick August 2026 and compare it with the
previous period.

14
00:00:49,497 --> 00:00:53,657
The Business Centre and the Residences
each show their income,

15
00:00:53,657 --> 00:00:57,816
expenses and NOI, with the change against
July beside them.

16
00:00:57,816 --> 00:01:01,560
Next, the Balance Sheet as at 31 August
2026.

17
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:05,719
PDC receivable, 165,985, is the paper
still in the drawer.

18
00:01:05,719 --> 00:01:09,879
Advance rent, 214,145.83, is rent billed
but not yet earned,

19
00:01:09,879 --> 00:01:14,038
and the 42,200 of security deposits are
held for tenants.

20
00:01:14,038 --> 00:01:16,950
Retained earnings carry the closed 2025
year,

21
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:19,861
and this year's result sits below them.

22
00:01:19,861 --> 00:01:23,189
Assets equal liabilities plus equity, in
every column.

23
00:01:23,189 --> 00:01:27,348
The Owner Statement gives one building's
month in a form

24
00:01:27,348 --> 00:01:31,508
you can send to its owner: income and NOI,
instalments

25
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:35,667
due, what was collected and what is
outstanding, deposits held

26
00:01:35,667 --> 00:01:39,411
and expenses, with a PDF in English or
Arabic.

27
00:01:39,411 --> 00:01:40,243
Finally, aging.

28
00:01:40,243 --> 00:01:43,986
Payables aging lists what is owed to each
supplier

29
00:01:43,986 --> 00:01:47,314
by days past due, as of any date,

30
00:01:47,314 --> 00:01:50,641
and ties every total to the supplier's
ledger.

31
00:01:50,641 --> 00:01:55,217
For tenants, the aging strip on Cheque and
Cash Collection sorts

32
00:01:55,217 --> 00:01:59,376
what is due by how many days it is
overdue.
